                url  :   &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Where Izzy Mandelbaum, an acquaintance of Morty and Helen's, takes Jerry &quot;aboard the pain train&quot; as his trash-talking personal trainer. Long closed, the site now handles &quot;doughboys&quot; of a different type as '''Carma East''', a ''dim sum'' restaurant. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#38</styleUrl>
                <Point id="913">
                    <coordinates>-73.983332,40.725342,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="916">
                <name>Country Cafe </name>
                <description>
                category  : Filming locations and places featured on the show_New York City_Manhattan &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 69 Thompson St., [[Manhattan/SoHo &lt;br&gt;
                url  :   &lt;br&gt;
                description  : &quot;You call yourself a lifesaver; I call you Pimple Popper, M.D.!&quot; Site of Jerry's &quot;revenge date&quot; with Sara, a dermatologist who, on an earlier date, had made Jerry feel &quot;like if [he doesn't] save lives, [he's] worthless&quot;. Country Cafe closed in 2010, but the current occupant of the space — classy French bistro '''[http://vinetfleurs.com/ Vin et Fleurs]''' — is still a great choice for all your revenge-dating needs. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#38</styleUrl>
