            <Placemark id="1066">
                <name>African Burial Ground National Monument </name>
                <description>
                category  : See_Museums &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 290 [[Broadway (street) &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://www.nps.gov/afbg  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : For most of the 18th century, Africans in New York City were buried in a graveyard outside the city. The graveyard was eventually forgotten and was rediscovered in 1991. This museum and memorial site commemorate the estimated 15,000 Africans that were interred on the site of the memorial. Note that the museum is located inside of a Federal building so airport-style security should be expected. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#122</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1065">
                    <coordinates>-74.0044,40.7144,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
