            <Placemark id="1368">
                <name>Washington Square Park </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  :   &lt;br&gt;
                url  : https://washingtonsquareparkconservancy.org  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : The park and its famous arch are located in the heart of the Village. Though located in the middle of an affluent neighborhood, the park attracts a hodgepodge of people. During the warmer months of the school term, the park is a favourite hangout spot for students from nearby NYU. Part of the charm of the park is the view of the buildings across the street. All these buildings are now owned by NYU, and though there has been some controversial construction in the early 2010s, most of the stately 19th-century dwellings pictured in the classic movie ''The Heiress'' (based on Henry James' novel, ''Washington Square'') are still there for you to enjoy looking at. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1367">
                    <coordinates>-73.9975,40.730833,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
