                url  : https://hamptoninn3.hilton.com/en/hotels/new-york/hampton-inn-manhattan-35th-st-empire-state-bldg-NYCEMHX/index.html  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : A business-style hotel with modern and clean rooms. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#106</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1745">
                    <coordinates>-73.98633,40.75038,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1748">
                <name>Bryant Park Hotel </name>
                <description>
                category  : Sleep_Splurge &lt;br&gt;
                address  : W 40th St  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://bryantparkhotel.com  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Distinctive black brick and gold trim building. Amenities include deep soaking tubs, cashmere blankets, Pipino toiletries, Tibetan rugs in rooms. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#106</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1747">
                    <coordinates>-73.98383,40.7528,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1750">
                <name>Official NYC Information Center at Macy's Herald Square </name>
                <description>
                category  : Understand_Visitor information &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 151 W. 34th St.  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://www.nycgo.com/venues/official-nyc-information-center-at-macys-herald-square-midtown-west  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Multilingual FAQ stations, free WiFi, plenty of guides and maps, and a MetroCard machine. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#38</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1749">
                    <coordinates>-73.98941,40.75072,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1752">
                <name>Times Square </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  : Broadway and 7th Avenue, stretching from 42nd to 48th Streets  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : https://www.timessquarenyc.org/  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : A place filled with video screens, LED signs, and flashing lights; a world wonder or a tourist nightmare depending on your perspective, the &quot;new&quot; Times Square is a family-friendly theme park of themed restaurants, theaters and hotels, as well as a developing business district. The lights and signs can be viewed anytime, but the most enchanting experience comes when one visits Times Square at night, as all the signs and screens are ablaze with color. Times Square is also well known for its famous New Year's Eve ball drop. Those looking for the seedy Times Square of years past will find it around the Port Authority Bus Terminal, and on Eighth Avenue to the west. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1751">
                    <coordinates>-73.985708,40.75773,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1754">
                <name>Rockefeller Center </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  :   &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://www.rockefellercenter.com  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : The Christmas Tree, the Skating Rink, NBC Studios, the shops and hubbub - you can't miss it. The Christmas Tree and the Skating Rink are naturally not year round, but in the summer, the complex is a hub for touristy operations. Within the striking Art Deco buildings of the complex are several dining establishments overlooking the area and many stores. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1753">
                    <coordinates>-73.979194,40.758611,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1756">
                <name>Museum of Modern Art </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 11 W 53rd St  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://moma.org/  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : One of the greatest and most popular collections of modern art, on a par with the Tate Modern in [[London]] or [[Paris]]'s Centre Georges Pompidou. Exceedingly popular so be warned: queues for tickets start early and stretch long. To avoid the crowds, turn up at the door ''at least'' a half hour before opening, then take the elevator to the top floor and work your way down. The building is as much a draw as the outstanding collection; possessing arguably the best collection of modern masterpieces world-wide, MoMA houses important art works from Van Gogh, Picasso, Monet, Matisse, Salvador Dalí, Paul Cézanne, Frida Kahlo, Piet Mondrian, and works by leading American artists such as Jackson Pollock, Jasper Johns, Edward Hopper, Andy Warhol, and Chuck Close. MoMA also holds renowned art photography and design collections. In addition to being the crown jewel of modern art museums, MoMA puts on a terrific repertory program in a nicely renovated theater below the museum. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1755">
                    <coordinates>-73.977664,40.761484,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1758">
                <name>Intrepid Sea, Air &amp; Space Museum </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  : Pier 86  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://www.intrepidmuseum.org/  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : The aircraft carrier ''Intrepid'' is docked here and loaded with spacecraft and aircraft, including the very cool Blackbird spy plane and the prototype Space Shuttle ''Enterprise''. On the other side of the dock is a guided-missile submarine and a Concorde, both of which you can tour also, and some tanks. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1757">
                    <coordinates>-74.000833,40.764722,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1760">
                <name>Madame Tussauds New York </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 234 W 42nd St  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://www.madametussauds.com/NewYork  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Get up close to over 200 lifelike wax figures of the biggest stars and icons in entertainment, sports and history. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1759">
                    <coordinates>-73.98825,40.75636,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1762">
                <name> Gulliver's Gate </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 216 W 44th St  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : https://gulliversgate.com/  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : A very large miniature world. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1761">
                    <coordinates>-73.986866,40.757633,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1764">
                <name>Saint Thomas Church </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 1 W. 53th St  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://www.saintthomaschurch.org  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : The interior of this Episcopal church is a peaceful place, and both the exterior and interior are architecturally harmonious and worth looking at if you are walking nearby. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1763">
                    <coordinates>-73.976111,40.760833,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1766">
                <name>The Paley Center for Media </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 25 W 52nd St  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://www.paleycenter.org/  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Dedicated to preserving and collecting television programs as a service to the public, the museum consists of two museum branches in Los Angeles and New York City; combined they hold over 100,000 television programs that are available to the public, providing a historical, artistic and cultural perspective to television and radio. You may use their library here for the price of admission. They have lots of old shows and a database so you can see if they have what you want. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1765">
                    <coordinates>-73.97759,40.76057,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1768">
                <name>Museum of Broadway </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 145 W 45th St  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : https://www.themuseumofbroadway.com  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Opened on November 15, 2022, this interactive museum utilizes technology to convey the history of Broadway, complete with props from past shows, costumes, and other artifacts. You can learn about how a Broadway show is made, and there is a gift shop selling not only their own merch, but also products from current Broadway shows and Broadway in general. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1767">
                    <coordinates>-73.984419,40.7575,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1770">
                <name>ABC Times Square Studios </name>
                <description>
                category  : Do &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 1500 Broadway  &lt;br&gt;
                url  :   &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Come here bright and early in the morning to be in the live audience of the network's famous morning news show, ''Good Morning America''. Walkbys can view the show in progress from the studio's street level windows and catch up on the latest news scrolling away continuously on the building's lower two message zippers. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#150</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1769">
                    <coordinates>-73.9857,40.75678,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
