                <description>
                category  : Eat_Budget &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 629 9th Ave  &lt;br&gt;
                url  :   &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Serves wonderful Greek pastries, savory and sweet alike. There is no place to sit, but the staff are very friendly and helpful, and you can have a delicious, cheap meal for takeout. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#82</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1811">
                    <coordinates>-73.99175,40.76008,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="1814">
                <name>The Halal Guys </name>
                <description>
                category  : Eat_Budget &lt;br&gt;
                address  : corner of 53rd Street and 6th Avenue  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://thehalalguys.com/  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : An extremely popular and affordable food stand that is probably the only Mediterranean stand in Manhattan that was given a name. This is the original location and since it started in 2008, it has begun a chain and opened 5 more throughout Manhattan and Bergen County, New Jersey. Delicious gyros, wraps, and falafel, and each dish comes with rice and pita bread. There's also an incredible white sauce that's worth trying. If you want some on a weekend, you're going to have to get there early because there is guaranteed to be a long wait. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#82</styleUrl>
                <Point id="1813">
                    <coordinates>-73.97928,40.76174,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
