            <Placemark id="2178">
                <name>Ansonia </name>
                <description>
                category  : See_Landmarks &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 2109 Broadway  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://ansoniarealty.com/  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : This pretty 17-story Beaux Arts building was completed in 1904 and designed to be New York City's first air conditioned hotel. It was a residential hotel, and housed a number of very famous people, including the Hall of Fame baseball player, Babe Ruth; the Italian tenor, Enrico Caruso; the modernist composer, Igor Stravinsky; the Italian conductor of the NBC Symphony, Arturo Toscanini; and writers Theodore Dreiser and Isaac Bashevis Singer. The building is now a condominium. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#118</styleUrl>
                <Point id="2177">
                    <coordinates>-73.9825,40.78,0.0</coordinates>
