            <Placemark id="2774">
                <name>Sewri Flamingo Point </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  :   &lt;br&gt;
                url  :   &lt;br&gt;
                description  : It has large areas of mudflats which are not only a safe habitat for flamingoes in winter but also have adequate food availability. A large number of flamingos reach along with their babies from their breeding area, Rann of Kutch, to Sewri every year. They arrive and stay between the month of October to March. Other bird species come to feed at the flats. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="2773">
                    <coordinates>72.86154968343902,18.995599650000003,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="2776">
                <name>Veermata Jijabai Bhosale Udyan </name>
                <description>
                category  : See &lt;br&gt;
                address  : Dr Babasaheb Ambedkar Rd, Byculla E  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://www.mcgm.gov.in/irj/portal/anonymous/qlrecpark  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : The zoo was established during British times and named &quot;Victoria Gardens&quot;. After India's independence, the zoo is renamed after Shivaji's mother Jijabai, though it is popularly known as '''Rani Baug''' (queen's garden). The place is not really worth visiting as it has been called more of a prison for animals than a zoo in the modern sense. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#110</styleUrl>
                <Point id="2775">
                    <coordinates>72.836746,18.978115,0.0</coordinates>
